            <ArticleTitle>Highly Diastereoselective Cationic Cyclization Reactions Convert a Common Monocyclic Enone to Bicyclic Precursors for the Synthesis of Retigeranic Acids A and B.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6686-6687</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03412</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel method is demonstrated for the diastereoselective conversion of a monocyclic enone to a pair of bicyclic intermediates which enable the stereocontrolled enantioselective syntheses of retigeranic acids A and B.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
